cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Organelle Direction: a signed readout of organelle dynamics from
  gene expression
message: >-
  If you use this software, the gene modules, or the results, please
  cite it using these metadata.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Taras
    family-names: Nazarov
    affiliation: >-
      Institute of Biological Chemistry, Washington State University
repository-code: 'https://github.com/different-change/organelle-direction'
abstract: >-
  Two cells can hold the same amount of an organelle for opposite
  reasons: one is building it, the other has blocked its clearance. A
  conventional single-axis organelle signature cannot separate those
  states, because build-up and tear-down move many of the same genes.
  This work scores the two opposing programs independently and
  subtracts them, giving one signed net_direction per sample from
  ordinary expression, proteomic or phosphoproteomic data. Across 1,066
  DepMap cancer cell lines the score predicts CRISPR mitochondrial
  dependency (rho = -0.35, p = 1.7e-32), survives burden and lineage
  controls, ranks mitochondria-targeting drugs to the top of a
  1,514-compound library without supervision, and beats raw expression
  on the same endpoint (AUROC 0.666 vs 0.613). Sixteen curated,
  provenance-tracked gene modules span seven organelles in yeast,
  Arabidopsis, rice and human. Nine directional predictions were
  recorded and hash-locked at the start of the validation work and
  reported together with their misses.
keywords:
  - organelle dynamics
  - selective autophagy
  - mitophagy
  - gene expression signature
  - DepMap
  - cancer dependency
  - organellomics
  - reproducible research
license: MIT
